  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/68F48E">Remark <span data-tag="68F48E">5.5.8.19</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be an $\infty $-category which admits geometric realizations of simplicial objects. Then the collection of projective objects of $\calC $ is stable under all finite coproducts which exist in $\calC $. This follows immediately from Lemma <a href="/tag/1F2E92" data-tag="1F2E92">5.5.8.11</a> and Remark <a href="/tag/71745F" data-tag="71745F">5.5.8.12</a>. </p>
